# Break MIDI (adaptive slices, docs/usage/adaptive-break-slices.md): every note on the
# break channel (default 4, status 0x93) wraps around C0 = MIDI 12: slice = (note - 12) mod A count.
# The default A count is 8. A note on the break channel must not also open a 303. midiheld bit 0 is the 303A gate.
wait 300
expect midiheld 0
expect noteons 0

# notes 36, 12 and 44 are all slice 0 at 8 slices. Releasing one leaves the others holding it.
midi 93 24 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0x100
midi 93 0C 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0x100
midi 83 0C 00 0
midi 93 2C 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0x100
midi 83 2C 00 0
midi 83 24 00 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0

# 303A moved onto channel 4. Break notes are consumed there and do not open the 303.
partch 2 4
midi 93 24 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0x100
midi 83 24 00 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0
midi 93 30 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0x1000
midi 83 30 00 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0
partch 2 2

# 303A on its own channel still plays. A drum-channel note 36 is not a break slice.
midi 91 30 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 1
midi 81 30 00 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0
midi 99 24 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0
midi 89 24 00 0

# notes 0 and 8 are slice 4 ((0 - 12) mod 8 and (8 - 12) mod 8). Releasing one leaves the other holding it.
midi 93 00 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0x1000
midi 93 08 64 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0x1000
midi 83 00 00 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0x1000
midi 83 08 00 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0

# a note off for a note that is not held changes nothing
midi 83 25 00 0
wait 20
expect midiheld 0
expect noteons 0
